   "explanation": {
    "en": "The embryo sac is 7-celled and 8-nucleate: an egg and two synergids at the micropylar end, three antipodals at the chalazal end and a large central cell with two polar nuclei. In double fertilisation one male gamete fuses with the egg (zygote) and the other with the polar nuclei (primary endosperm nucleus, 3n)."
   },
