  {
   "id": "concept2",
   "type": "concept",
   "title": {
    "en": "Embryo sac and double fertilisation"
   },
   "body": {
    "en": "Inside each ovule is a seven-celled embryo sac: an egg apparatus of one egg and two synergids, three antipodal cells and two polar nuclei that fuse into a diploid secondary nucleus. The pollen tube brings two male gametes. One fuses with the egg (syngamy) to form the zygote; the other fuses with the secondary nucleus (triple fusion) to form the triploid primary endosperm nucleus. This double fertilisation is unique to angiosperms.",
    "kn": "ಭ್ರೂಣಕೋಶದಲ್ಲಿ ಅಂಡ, ಎರಡು ಸಿನರ್ಜಿಡ್‌ಗಳು, ಮೂರು ಪ್ರತಿಪಾದ ಕೋಶಗಳು ಮತ್ತು ದ್ವಿತೀಯಕ ಕೋಶಕೇಂದ್ರ. ಒಂದು ಪುರುಷ ಗ್ಯಾಮೀಟ್ ಅಂಡದೊಂದಿಗೆ (ಯುಗ್ಮನ), ಇನ್ನೊಂದು ದ್ವಿತೀಯಕ ಕೋಶಕೇಂದ್ರದೊಂದಿಗೆ (ತ್ರಿಸಂಯೋಗ). ಇದೇ ದ್ವಿಫಲೀಕರಣ."
   },
   "points": [
    {
     "en": "Egg apparatus: egg + 2 synergids"
    },
    {
     "en": "Syngamy → zygote (2n)"
    },
    {
     "en": "Triple fusion → PEN (3n) → endosperm"
    },
    {
